Sol-Floorwright: Lares (Tasked Spirit), Ink-Clerk: ->✶ ''1. Measured ground, span head.'' MEASURED: Road names W14–W16 and the rotation/carry witness [[stable-founding-road.mem:506–514|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem#L506]].

| Row | Writers and readers today |h
| W14 | Node banner derives `/flow` pin and publisher from its vessel identity, then serializes `#floor=` [[main.ts:723–743|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/main.ts#L723]], [[hearth-floor-pins.ts:78–105|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/hearth-floor-pins.ts#L78]]. Web parses fragment and passes text into browser vessel [[main.ts:342–395|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-web/src/main.ts#L342]]; browser shape-reads and files pin [[open-browser-vessel.ts:806–816|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts#L806]]. No card signature verifies. Browser reads porch by card/admit AID, verifies release lineage and CID bytes, yet records no accepted head [[browser-floor-read.ts:4–15,43–68|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-floor-read.ts#L4]]; node porch emits board releases [[floor-porch.ts:78–96|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/floor-porch.ts#L78]], mesh checks lineage, release chain and blobs [[floor-answer.ts:62–96|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/floor-answer.ts#L62]]. |
| W15 | Place signs `{kind,placeKey,pin,sig}`; image binds coordinates/digest, not position [[place-floor-pin.ts:50–81|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts#L50]]. Reader checks signature and counted carrier, board writer overwrites one sidecar per place, extractor reads all, filer calls `put` [[place-floor-pin.ts:88–153|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/place-floor-pin.ts#L88]]. Herm refresh signs/lays, then reads board and files [[herm-carriage.ts:68–106|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/herm-carriage.ts#L68]]. Index keys `(hearth,Nexus,route,tier)` and accepts the first digest until drop [[admit-gate-pin.ts:84–134|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/admit-gate-pin.ts#L84]]. Node seeds it from bootstrap/admit and kept floor pins [[hearth-gate-pins.ts:69–123|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/hearth-gate-pins.ts#L69]]; browser seeds from fleet join and card [[browser-gate-pins.ts:18–45,77–85|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-gate-pins.ts#L18]]. Verified sovereign session also files floor set via adapter [[lar-ws-client-adapter.ts:365–385|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-ws-client-adapter.ts#L365]]. |
| W16 | `carry-for` signs a place pin; one-vault `landEntry` writes act plus supplied statement [[nexus-contract.ts:245–280,349–366|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts#L245]]. Partial gate allows admit/revoke alone and landing sets `floorPin:null` [[nexus-contract.ts:450–509|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/commands/nexus-contract.ts#L450]]. Carry bundle exports board statements; herm take verifies counted acts and eligible statements, then writes both [[carry-bundle.ts:54–69,114–160|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/carry-bundle.ts#L54]]. A herm can lay its own statement during refresh [[herm-carriage.ts:80–89|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/herm-carriage.ts#L80]]; current two-vault contract door still blocks its carry. |

Sol-Floorwright: Lares (Tasked Spirit), Map-Wisp: ->⏿ ''3. One shape.'' LEAD: name ''floor standing'': `place carries floor standing at Nexus, route and causal head`. Extend the ''place KEL'', then bind each pin statement and card to its verified key-state head `(place AID, sequence, event CID)` and the exact gate pin digest. A release head may accompany the card as evidence of floor content, yet the release record governs canon, not place-key rotation. The edge frontier governs raises, not keys. The card signer should follow the place KEL current scoped signer; the Nexus AID anchors charter/release verification, never signs a household gate key. A herm signs its own standing; the counted `carry` authorizes that place and Nexus. LEAD: make the card carry AID, place identity, KEL proof/head, pin, publisher, domain-separated signature; verify the signed binding before any pin filing. First contact still needs an independently conveyed anchor (genesis, authenticated admit, or person's deliberate card transfer); self-signature alone cannot bless an attacker-supplied place.

MEASURED canon already rules: “a pin moves only by a signed causal event or a verified key-history step, and no quiet period ages a pin out” [[road:219|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem#L219]]; the place signer sits under a pre-rotated KEL, though code still commits no next key [[road:207|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem#L207]]; edge frontier signs board boundaries [[road:256|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem#L256]]; herm carries without signing release [[road:195|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem#L195]]. LEAD, still unruled: which place anchor card readers trust, whether cards require current KEL head or accept a proven older one, how equal-sequence forks resolve, where each vessel persists its highest head, and whether a floor-pin change without place-key rotation needs its own signed successor event. Index should replace only on a proven descendant position; equal-position divergent digests refuse and surface conflict. Session/admit/card/board carriers should all pass the same verifier and monotone index; live refresh should notify active dials and re-file without restart.

Sol-Floorwright: Lares (Tasked Spirit), Ink-Clerk: ->◇ ''2. Prior art and limit.'' KERI offers pre-rotation, sequence plus event digest and witnesses; local verification of a KEL fits, while a compulsory global witness set would alter this house's topology ([[KERI specification|https://trustoverip.github.io/kswg-keri-specification/]]). TUF separates signed root, snapshot and timestamp; its expiry-based freeze defense needs a clock, so a held causal head plus explicit sync/accept act replaces timestamp only for ''known'' rollback, not unseen withholding ([[TUF specification|https://theupdateframework.github.io/specification/v1.0.36/]]). CT consistency proofs and Sigstore Rekor log inclusion can expose forks after gossip; neither tells an isolated phone that a newer head exists ([[RFC 9162|https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9162]], [[Sigstore Rekor|https://docs.sigstore.dev/logging/overview/]]). DNSSEC RFC 5011 relies on timed hold-down; that move violates no-global-now ([[RFC 5011|https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5011]]). SSH `UpdateHostKeys` learns replacements after authenticating a trusted host, a useful trust-path analogy; WireGuard rotates session keys, not the pinned place identity ([[OpenSSH manual|https://man.openbsd.org/OpenBSD-8.0/ssh_config.5]], [[WireGuard paper|https://www.wireguard.com/papers/wireguard.pdf]]).

Sol-Floorwright: Lares (Tasked Spirit), Map-Wisp: ->▶ ''5. Witness stories.'' Gaia: hearth rotates floor key while phone rests offline. Phone reconnects with pinned KEL head; old card fails ''after'' it receives the descendant proof, and new signed standing re-files live. Before that proof, phone can only say “as of my last sync”; absolute rejection of an unseen rotation cannot follow from clockless local evidence. Elyncia: two shrines cosign a `carry` partial containing the waystone's signed floor standing; the landing board commits act and standing together. Herm takes the bundle, verifies counted carry, writes no authority of its own, stands its gate, and relays bytes without reading them. Storm control: permute old/new card, session set, carry bundle and restart across node/browser; every carrier with the same verified head chooses the same pin, never regresses, and reports a fork rather than selecting by arrival order.

Sol-Floorwright: Lares (Tasked Spirit), Lares (Artificer): ->↺ ''6. Lane kit, red first.'' 1. Pin-position verifier and index in `mesh/{place-floor-pin,admit-gate-pin,hearth-floor-pins}`: red for rollback, same-position fork and wrong Nexus; positive descendant advances, negative stale never files. 2. Signed card plus trusted anchor through `node/{main,lan-address}`, `web/{main,live-status}`, `browser/{open-browser-vessel,browser-floor-read,browser-gate-pins}`: red forged card, swapped AID and withheld proof; positive valid first arrival reads porch. 3. Live refiling through `node/{hearth-gate-pins,herm-carriage,open-node-vessel}`, mesh session adapter and browser composer: red rotation during open vessel; positive new dial and silent-zero counter with known positive. 4. Two-vault carry through `node/commands/nexus-contract`, `carry-bundle`, mesh partial type/judge and carriage board: red partial with missing, stale or foreign standing; positive cosign lands act and pin atomically, herm take/dial succeeds. 5. Storm across node/browser with offline replay and opposing arrival orders; require convergence ''after shared evidence''. K17-R owns lease law and realm boards; consume its frontier verifier without editing those files. W28 owns `gate-exchange`, `face-gate*`, `face-dial`; avoid frame edits. X0 place-KEL bake gates card signer semantics [[road:544|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem#L544]]. Operator choices: card anchor—place KEL via genesis/admit/person transfer (lean) or Nexus charter delegation; fork—refuse and expose (lean) or deterministic winner; no-head offline dial—hold last accepted pin (lean, matching canon) or suspend; key rotation position—KEL head plus signed per-route successor (lean) or release head. Build only after these rulings; no interim carrier format.

&lt;&lt;~ oracle "↯16 ✲ ⚂(3) ⁂:🜃⌗◈">>
